# Track 6 Item 3 — Canary Windows capability safety hardening — COMPLETE

Date: 2026-09-19
Branch: `build/initial-product`
Status when written: official application GREEN; exact documentary-HEAD Windows CI pending.

## Why this bounded regression was needed

A declared `GuardianAction` marked `LiveSafe` passed the generic canary's eligibility/preflight even when its separate `WindowsMutationRequest.CapabilityId` identified a `LobbySafe` Windows capability. The read-only eligibility/action metadata was not the Windows capability authority. The generic host is still not wired, but this gap had to be closed before runtime integration.

## TDD evidence

Verifier branch: `ci/track6-canary-capability-safety-verify` (temporary workflow excluded from official branch).
- RED test registered in `tests/FFPerformanceEngine.Core.SelfTest/Program.cs`, test source `GenericGuardianLiveSafeCapabilitySelfTests.cs`; RED SHA `3dfa8e3ade2d1ffe4b2c48fa8fb121ae90cf302f`; verifier run `35424479978`, job `105847961374`, FAILURE as intended. Native configure/build/test and managed build SUCCESS (0 compile warnings/errors). Existing Core tests passed until new test failed: `Unsafe or unknown capability test.lobby must fail preflight before any measurement or mutation.` The old executor reached fake typed capture for `LobbySafe`.
- GREEN verifier SHA `b28e13b3cd7aed3ae47147a7ffb26915008d0861`; run `35424662173`, job `105848430682`, SUCCESS for native configure/build/test, managed, Core self-tests including the new test, App self-tests and Windows publish.

## Minimal production contract

- `SystemOptimizationTransactionEngine.IsLiveSafeSessionCapability` reads the existing authoritative capability registry and returns true only for an existing, currently Available, session-applicable `ActionSafety.LiveSafe` capability. It creates no mutation rights; BeginSession still owns fresh validation/snapshot/apply/rollback.
- `GenericGuardianWindowsSessionCanaryExecutor.PreflightFailure` checks this authority against the exact bound Windows mutation *before* typed before-capture. Candidate Action.LiveSafe is not enough.
- Regression tests reject `LobbySafe`, `RestartRequired` and unknown capabilities with zero captures, zero mutations; a real LiveSafe descriptor may reach before-capture, where absent evidence still forbids mutation.
- No Guardian host wiring, learning, profile/recommendation authority, startup discovery, UI, or Global Controlled Benchmark Lease semantics added.

